<title>RUSSIA: Russian freighters may carry aid to Zaire.</title>
<headline>Russian freighters may carry aid to Zaire.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 30 Russian Ilyushin-76TD freighters may be used to deliver aid to Zaire, a Moscow-based freight forwarder said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Chapman Freeborn Russia's manager Chris Lewis told Reuters that his company hoped to lease the cargo aircraft.</p>
<p>&quot;We are in talks with the United Nations about leasing 30 Il-76TD planes for delivery of humanitarian cargoes from France to Zaire,&quot; said Lewis, whose company is a unit of British-based Chapman Freeborn. He did not say which Russian airlines were involved in the talks.</p>
<p>-- Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
